{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":58650,"ns":0,"title":"Base unit of measurement","extract":"A base unit of measurement (also referred to as a base unit or fundamental unit) is a unit of measurement adopted for a base quantity. A base quantity is one of a conventionally chosen subset of physical quantities, where no quantity in the subset can be expressed in terms of the others.","description":"Unit of measurement adopted by convention for a base quantity","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}